(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Digital mental health interventions show promise for anxiety disorders, yet) Tj
T*
(adherence and durability of clinical gains remain uncertain. This protocol describes a) Tj
T*
(prospective evaluation of a behavioral-flexibility-focused smartphone application combined) Tj
T*
(with routine care versus routine care alone. Methods: We will randomize 96 individuals) Tj
T*
(\(aged >=19 years\) with diagnosed generalized anxiety disorder to receive either the active) Tj
T*
(intervention plus standard support or standard support alone. The intervention period will) Tj
T*
(span 10 weeks, with follow-up assessment at week 15. Outcome evaluators will remain masked) Tj
T*
(to treatment allocation. The primary metric will be change in standardized anxiety) Tj
T*
(severity scales from baseline to intervention endpoint. Secondary measures will capture) Tj
T*
(worry frequency and mood symptoms. We will also track adherence through in-app engagement) Tj
T*
(metrics and assess acceptability. Data collection will occur at baseline, mid-intervention) Tj
T*
(\(week 5\), post-intervention \(week 10\), and follow-up \(week 15\).) Tj
